<Ui>
    <!--
        benilla's guild registrar (decision 1672) — the window the "How do I form a guild?" gossip
        row opens, and the only place a guild charter can be bought or turned in.

        The geometry and art are the real `GuildRegistrarFrame.xml`'s (extracted at
        `WoW/_extracted_framexml/GuildRegistrarFrame.{xml,lua}`; `ref l.N` cites are into those).
        Every global, frame name, event, texture, string and number below is the reference's and is
        the contract addons bind to (1260's rule, still the rule after 1602 retired the
        transcription gate): what is ours is the expression — named functions instead of inline
        handler bodies, the service rows over one small local template, and this comment.

        TWO PANELS ON ONE CHROME, exactly as the reference has it (ref l.116, l.196):

          GUILD_REGISTRAR_SHOW   → the window opens on GuildRegistrarGreetingFrame — the two
                                   service rows, "Purchase a Guild Charter" and "Register a Guild
                                   Charter".
          Purchase clicked       → GuildRegistrarPurchaseFrame swaps in: the explanatory text, the
                                   cost, and the guild-name box. NOT a second window and NOT a
                                   server round trip — `GuildRegistrar_ShowPurchaseFrame` is a pure
                                   local swap (ref l.8-12).
          GUILD_REGISTRAR_CLOSED → the window hides.

        WHY THE COST IS READ AT PANEL-SWAP TIME AND NOT AT SHOW TIME: the reference calls
        `MoneyFrame_Update("GuildRegistrarMoneyFrame", GetGuildCharterCost())` inside
        `GuildRegistrar_ShowPurchaseFrame` (ref l.10) — the greeting panel never displays a price.
        Ours does the same, and it matters here: `GetGuildCharterCost()` answers from the *open
        registrar's* showlist row, so reading it before a registrar is open would paint a 0.

        THE WINDOW IS NOT SELF-CLOSING ON PURCHASE BY ACCIDENT. Both the Purchase button and the
        edit box's Enter key hide the whole panel after sending (ref l.253-257, l.312-315) — a buy
        is one-shot, and the charter arrives as an item rather than as any answer to this window.
        That is the reference's own behaviour and it is quoted, not invented.

        UIPanel slot system (decision 0084 §2): carries NO hardcoded <Anchors> — ShowUIPanel seats
        it in the left slot from `UIPanelWindows["GuildRegistrarFrame"]` (UiPanels.xml), which is
        the reference's own registration (`UIParent.lua:33`, area="left", pushable=0). Hiding it
        goes through HideUIPanel so the slot is released and ESC reaches it.
    -->

    <Script><![CDATA[
        -- ── The registrar's strings (GlobalStrings.lua, verbatim) ──────────────────────────────
        -- The `text=` attributes below name these KEYS rather than spelling the words, which is
        -- what the reference's own XML does and what the loader resolves (0991). In a real session
        -- the app has already run the shipped GlobalStrings.lua, so these lines are the
        -- standalone-load copy — same values, same file, line numbers named. `X = X or "…"`
        -- throughout, never a bare `=`, for FriendsFrame.xml's reason: CANCEL and PURCHASE are
        -- generic names the real string table already owns, and a bare assignment would overwrite
        -- the shipped value with this copy on every load.
        AVAILABLE_SERVICES = AVAILABLE_SERVICES or "Available Services"           -- l.128
        COSTS_LABEL = COSTS_LABEL or "Cost:"                                      -- l.870
        PURCHASE = PURCHASE or "Purchase"                                         -- l.3128
        CANCEL = CANCEL or "Cancel"                                               -- l.465
        GUILD_CHARTER_PURCHASE = GUILD_CHARTER_PURCHASE or "Purchase a Guild Charter" -- l.2058
        GUILD_CHARTER_REGISTER = GUILD_CHARTER_REGISTER or "Register a Guild Charter" -- l.2059
        GUILD_REGISTRAR_PURCHASE_TEXT = GUILD_REGISTRAR_PURCHASE_TEXT or "To create a guild you must purchase this charter, get 9 unique player signatures, and return the charter to me.  Please enter the desired name for your guild." -- l.2107

        -- ref GuildRegistrarFrame.lua:1-6. Every show starts on the services list: the purchase
        -- panel is a transient sub-view, so re-opening the window must not land on a half-filled
        -- name box from last time.
        function GuildRegistrar_OnShow()
            GuildRegistrarGreetingFrame:Show()
            GuildRegistrarPurchaseFrame:Hide()
            SetPortraitTexture(GuildRegistrarFramePortrait, "npc")
            GuildRegistrarFrameNpcNameText:SetText(UnitName("npc"))
        end

        -- ref GuildRegistrarFrame.lua:8-12. A pure local panel swap — no packet, no round trip.
        -- The cost is read HERE rather than on show because this is the only panel that displays
        -- one (see the file header).
        function GuildRegistrar_ShowPurchaseFrame()
            GuildRegistrarPurchaseFrame:Show()
            GuildRegistrarGreetingFrame:Hide()
            MoneyFrame_Update("GuildRegistrarMoneyFrame", GetGuildCharterCost())
        end

        -- The buy, shared by the Purchase button and the box's Enter key (ref l.253-257 and
        -- l.312-315, which carry the same three lines twice). Hiding the panel after sending is
        -- the reference's own behaviour: a buy is one-shot and its answer is an item arriving, not
        -- anything this window will be told.
        function GuildRegistrar_Purchase(name)
            BuyGuildCharter(name)
            HideUIPanel(GuildRegistrarFrame)
            GuildRegistrar_RefocusChat()
        end

        -- The reference indexes `ChatFrameEditBox` bare (ref l.256, l.314, l.317). Ours nil-guards
        -- it, this house's convention everywhere it is touched from outside ChatFrame.xml
        -- (FriendsFrame.xml's four dialogs, BagFrame.xml) — an unguarded index is a real error line
        -- for anyone who loads this window without the chat frame, which the reference never has to
        -- consider because there FrameXML is all-or-nothing. The refocus itself stays
        -- UNCONDITIONAL when the box exists: the popups' extra `IsVisible()` test is a rule about
        -- dialogs, not about this window, and borrowing it would change behaviour rather than
        -- harden it.
        function GuildRegistrar_RefocusChat()
            if ChatFrameEditBox then
                ChatFrameEditBox:SetFocus()
            end
        end

        -- ref l.318-327. The show arm's `IsVisible` re-test is the reference's own: ShowUIPanel can
        -- refuse (another window owns the slot, or the player is dead), and a registrar session the
        -- server thinks is open with no window on screen is a stuck NPC — so the client closes it
        -- back out immediately.
        function GuildRegistrar_OnEvent(event)
            if event == "GUILD_REGISTRAR_SHOW" then
                ShowUIPanel(GuildRegistrarFrame)
                if not GuildRegistrarFrame:IsVisible() then
                    CloseGuildRegistrar()
                end
            elseif event == "GUILD_REGISTRAR_CLOSED" then
                HideUIPanel(GuildRegistrarFrame)
            end
        end
    ]]></Script>

    <!-- One service row (ref inherits="QuestTitleButtonTemplate", QuestFrameTemplates.xml l.174-213):
         a bullet plus the service name. Local rather than QuestFrame.xml's
         `BenillaQuestTitleButtonTemplate` because that one hardwires `QuestTitleButton_OnClick()`
         and would drag this window's load order behind the questgiver's for a fifteen-line shape.
         Same LEFT-anchored title as that template, and for the same reason: the round bullet is
         cell-centred, so a TOPLEFT-anchored label rides above it (QuestFrame.xml's own note). -->
    <Button name="BenillaGuildRegistrarServiceTemplate" virtual="true" hidden="true">
        <Size><AbsDimension x="285" y="16"/></Size>
        <Layers>
            <Layer level="BACKGROUND">
                <Texture file="Interface\QuestFrame\UI-Quest-BulletPoint">
                    <Size><AbsDimension x="16" y="16"/></Size>
                    <Anchors><Anchor point="TOPLEFT" relativePoint="TOPLEFT"/></Anchors>
                </Texture>
            </Layer>
        </Layers>
        <HighlightTexture file="Interface\QuestFrame\UI-QuestTitleHighlight" alphaMode="ADD"/>
        <ButtonText>
            <Size><AbsDimension x="275" y="0"/></Size>
            <Anchors><Anchor point="LEFT" relativePoint="LEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="20" y="0"/></Offset></Anchor></Anchors>
        </ButtonText>
        <NormalFont inherits="QuestFont" justifyH="LEFT"/>
    </Button>

    <Frame name="GuildRegistrarFrame" toplevel="true" parent="UIParent" movable="true" enableMouse="true" hidden="true">
        <Size><AbsDimension x="384" y="512"/></Size>
        <!-- ref l.16-19: the window's own dead zone at the right edge and along the bottom, so a
             drag on the parchment's painted border does not grab the window. -->
        <HitRectInsets><AbsInset left="0" right="30" top="0" bottom="70"/></HitRectInsets>
        <Layers>
            <Layer level="BACKGROUND">
                <!-- The NPC's face (ref l.21-31), filled by SetPortraitTexture on show. -->
                <Texture name="GuildRegistrarFramePortrait">
                    <Size><AbsDimension x="60" y="60"/></Size>
                    <Anchors><Anchor point="TOPLEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="7" y="-6"/></Offset></Anchor></Anchors>
                </Texture>
            </Layer>
            <Layer level="ARTWORK">
                <!-- The quest-greeting parchment, four quadrant slabs (ref l.34-65) — the same art
                     GossipFrame and QuestFrame wear, at the same 384x512. -->
                <Texture file="Interface\QuestFrame\UI-QuestGreeting-TopLeft">
                    <Size><AbsDimension x="256" y="256"/></Size>
                    <Anchors><Anchor point="TOPLEFT"/></Anchors>
                </Texture>
                <Texture file="Interface\QuestFrame\UI-QuestGreeting-TopRight">
                    <Size><AbsDimension x="128" y="256"/></Size>
                    <Anchors><Anchor point="TOPRIGHT"/></Anchors>
                </Texture>
                <Texture file="Interface\QuestFrame\UI-QuestGreeting-BotLeft">
                    <Size><AbsDimension x="256" y="256"/></Size>
                    <Anchors><Anchor point="BOTTOMLEFT"/></Anchors>
                </Texture>
                <Texture file="Interface\QuestFrame\UI-QuestGreeting-BotRight">
                    <Size><AbsDimension x="128" y="256"/></Size>
                    <Anchors><Anchor point="BOTTOMRIGHT"/></Anchors>
                </Texture>
                <!-- ref l.66-79. Defined but never written by the shipped UI; kept because it is a
                     name an addon can reach. -->
                <FontString name="GuildRegistrarText" inherits="QuestFont" justifyH="LEFT">
                    <Size><AbsDimension x="270" y="0"/></Size>
                    <Anchors><Anchor point="TOPLEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="10" y="-10"/></Offset></Anchor></Anchors>
                </FontString>
            </Layer>
        </Layers>
        <Frames>
            <!-- The title banner (ref l.83-107): the NPC's name, two frame levels above the
                 parchment so it is not painted over. -->
            <Frame name="GuildRegistrarNpcNameFrame">
                <Size><AbsDimension x="300" y="14"/></Size>
                <Anchors>
                    <Anchor point="TOP" relativeTo="GuildRegistrarFrame" relativePoint="TOP"><Offset><AbsDimension x="0" y="-23"/></Offset></Anchor>
                </Anchors>
                <Layers>
                    <Layer level="BACKGROUND">
                        <FontString name="GuildRegistrarFrameNpcNameText" inherits="GameFontHighlight"/>
                    </Layer>
                </Layers>
                <Scripts>
                    <OnLoad>this:SetFrameLevel(this:GetFrameLevel() + 2)</OnLoad>
                </Scripts>
            </Frame>

            <Button name="GuildRegistrarFrameCloseButton" inherits="UIPanelCloseButton">
                <Anchors>
                    <Anchor point="CENTER" relativeTo="GuildRegistrarFrame" relativePoint="TOPRIGHT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="-42" y="-30"/></Offset></Anchor>
                </Anchors>
            </Button>

            <!-- ── Panel 1: the services list ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <Frame name="GuildRegistrarGreetingFrame" setAllPoints="true" hidden="true">
                <Layers>
                    <Layer level="BACKGROUND">
                        <FontString name="AvailableServicesText" inherits="QuestTitleFont" text="AVAILABLE_SERVICES" justifyH="LEFT">
                            <Size><AbsDimension x="300" y="0"/></Size>
                            <Anchors><Anchor point="TOPLEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="35" y="-100"/></Offset></Anchor></Anchors>
                        </FontString>
                        <!-- The torn-parchment patch along the bottom edge (ref l.127-138). -->
                        <Texture file="Interface\QuestFrame\UI-Quest-BotLeftPatch">
                            <Size><AbsDimension x="128" y="64"/></Size>
                            <Anchors><Anchor point="BOTTOMLEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="22" y="68"/></Offset></Anchor></Anchors>
                        </Texture>
                    </Layer>
                </Layers>
                <Frames>
                    <Button name="GuildRegistrarFrameGoodbyeButton" inherits="UIPanelButtonTemplate" text="CANCEL">
                        <Size><AbsDimension x="75" y="22"/></Size>
                        <Anchors>
                            <Anchor point="BOTTOMRIGHT" relativeTo="GuildRegistrarFrame" relativePoint="BOTTOMRIGHT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="-40" y="72"/></Offset></Anchor>
                        </Anchors>
                        <Scripts><OnClick>HideUIPanel(GuildRegistrarFrame)</OnClick></Scripts>
                    </Button>
                    <Button name="GuildRegistrarButton1" inherits="BenillaGuildRegistrarServiceTemplate" text="GUILD_CHARTER_PURCHASE">
                        <Anchors>
                            <Anchor point="TOPLEFT" relativeTo="AvailableServicesText" relativePoint="BOTTOMLEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="-10" y="-10"/></Offset></Anchor>
                        </Anchors>
                        <Scripts><OnClick>GuildRegistrar_ShowPurchaseFrame()</OnClick></Scripts>
                    </Button>
                    <Button name="GuildRegistrarButton2" inherits="BenillaGuildRegistrarServiceTemplate" text="GUILD_CHARTER_REGISTER">
                        <Anchors>
                            <Anchor point="TOPLEFT" relativeTo="GuildRegistrarButton1" relativePoint="BOTTOMLEFT"/>
                        </Anchors>
                        <!-- Turn the charter in. Takes no argument: the engine finds the charter in
                             the bags, because the wire wants an item guid and Lua has no way to
                             name one. A player with no charter gets ERR_NO_GUILD_CHARTER and no
                             packet leaves (`ui_petition::feed`'s drain). -->
                        <Scripts><OnClick>TurnInGuildCharter()</OnClick></Scripts>
                    </Button>
                    <!-- The reference's third row, "Design a Guild Crest", is COMMENTED OUT in the
                         shipped file (ref l.183-194) and its `GUILD_CREST_DESIGN` string does not
                         exist in 1.12's GlobalStrings — tabard design runs off its own NPC gossip
                         option, not this window. Not shipped here either, deliberately: the
                         reference's own dead code is not a gap to fill. -->
                </Frames>
            </Frame>

            <!-- ── Panel 2: buy a charter ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <Frame name="GuildRegistrarPurchaseFrame" setAllPoints="true" hidden="true">
                <Layers>
                    <Layer level="ARTWORK">
                        <FontString name="GuildRegistrarPurchaseText" inherits="QuestFont" text="GUILD_REGISTRAR_PURCHASE_TEXT" justifyH="LEFT">
                            <Size><AbsDimension x="270" y="0"/></Size>
                            <Anchors><Anchor point="TOPLEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="35" y="-95"/></Offset></Anchor></Anchors>
                        </FontString>
                        <FontString name="GuildRegistrarCostLabel" inherits="GameFontNormal" text="COSTS_LABEL">
                            <Anchors>
                                <Anchor point="TOPLEFT" relativeTo="GuildRegistrarPurchaseText" relativePoint="BOTTOMLEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="0" y="-5"/></Offset></Anchor>
                            </Anchors>
                        </FontString>
                    </Layer>
                </Layers>
                <Frames>
                    <!-- The shared money kit (MoneyFrame.xml), STATIC type — a read-only price, no
                         click-to-edit. GetGuildCharterCost() answers in copper, which is this
                         kit's whole vocabulary. -->
                    <Frame name="GuildRegistrarMoneyFrame" inherits="MoneyFrameTemplate">
                        <Anchors>
                            <Anchor point="LEFT" relativeTo="GuildRegistrarCostLabel" relativePoint="RIGHT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="15" y="0"/></Offset></Anchor>
                        </Anchors>
                        <Scripts>
                            <OnLoad>
                                MoneyFrame_OnLoad()
                                MoneyFrame_SetType("STATIC")
                            </OnLoad>
                        </Scripts>
                    </Frame>
                    <Button name="GuildRegistrarFrameCancelButton" inherits="UIPanelButtonTemplate" text="CANCEL">
                        <Size><AbsDimension x="75" y="22"/></Size>
                        <Anchors>
                            <Anchor point="BOTTOMRIGHT" relativeTo="GuildRegistrarFrame" relativePoint="BOTTOMRIGHT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="-40" y="72"/></Offset></Anchor>
                        </Anchors>
                        <Scripts><OnClick>HideUIPanel(GuildRegistrarFrame)</OnClick></Scripts>
                    </Button>
                    <Button name="GuildRegistrarFramePurchaseButton" inherits="UIPanelButtonTemplate" text="PURCHASE">
                        <Size><AbsDimension x="85" y="22"/></Size>
                        <Anchors>
                            <Anchor point="BOTTOMLEFT" relativeTo="GuildRegistrarFrame"><Offset><AbsDimension x="22" y="72"/></Offset></Anchor>
                        </Anchors>
                        <Scripts><OnClick>GuildRegistrar_Purchase(GuildRegistrarFrameEditBox:GetText())</OnClick></Scripts>
                    </Button>
                    <!-- 24 letters is the server's own MAX_CHARTER_NAME, so the box cannot compose
                         a name the server will reject for length (ref l.271). -->
                    <EditBox name="GuildRegistrarFrameEditBox" letters="24" historyLines="1">
                        <Size><AbsDimension x="130" y="32"/></Size>
                        <Anchors>
                            <Anchor point="TOPLEFT" relativeTo="GuildRegistrarCostLabel" relativePoint="BOTTOMLEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="0" y="-5"/></Offset></Anchor>
                        </Anchors>
                        <Layers>
                            <Layer level="BACKGROUND">
                                <Texture file="Interface\ChatFrame\UI-ChatInputBorder-Left">
                                    <Size><AbsDimension x="75" y="32"/></Size>
                                    <Anchors><Anchor point="LEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="-10" y="0"/></Offset></Anchor></Anchors>
                                    <TexCoords left="0" right="0.29296875" top="0" bottom="1.0"/>
                                </Texture>
                                <Texture file="Interface\ChatFrame\UI-ChatInputBorder-Right">
                                    <Size><AbsDimension x="75" y="32"/></Size>
                                    <Anchors><Anchor point="RIGHT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="10" y="0"/></Offset></Anchor></Anchors>
                                    <TexCoords left="0.70703125" right="1.0" top="0" bottom="1.0"/>
                                </Texture>
                            </Layer>
                        </Layers>
                        <Scripts>
                            <OnEnterPressed>GuildRegistrar_Purchase(this:GetText())</OnEnterPressed>
                            <OnEscapePressed>GuildRegistrar_RefocusChat()</OnEscapePressed>
                        </Scripts>
                        <FontString inherits="ChatFontNormal"/>
                    </EditBox>
                </Frames>
            </Frame>
        </Frames>
        <Scripts>
            <OnLoad>
                this:RegisterEvent("GUILD_REGISTRAR_SHOW")
                this:RegisterEvent("GUILD_REGISTRAR_CLOSED")
            </OnLoad>
            <OnEvent>GuildRegistrar_OnEvent(event)</OnEvent>
            <OnShow>
                GuildRegistrar_OnShow()
                PlaySound("igQuestListOpen")
            </OnShow>
            <!-- CloseGuildRegistrar() on hide is load-bearing, not tidiness: it is what clears the
                 engine's registrar session, so the next GUILD_REGISTRAR_SHOW is a real open (and
                 GetGuildCharterCost() stops quoting a price for a registrar nobody is talking to).
                 Same shape as GossipFrame's CloseGossip(). -->
            <OnHide>
                PlaySound("igQuestListClose")
                CloseGuildRegistrar()
            </OnHide>
        </Scripts>
    </Frame>
</Ui>
